_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 11
---
order: 11
---
short_label: X.11
---
statement: If four magnitudes are proportional, and the first is commensurable with the second, then the third also is commensurable with the fourth; but, if the first is incommensurable with the second, then the third also is incommensurable with the fourth.
---
proof:

---
body:

